{
  "paper_id": "nar2026-gkag794",
  "title": "Sequential-GAM constructs the single-cell geometric 3D genome structure.",
  "doi": "10.1093/nar/gkag794",
  "journal": "Nucleic Acids Research",
  "data_url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE193989",
  "verified": {
    "opened_data_files": true,
    "what_i_actually_checked": "Downloaded and parsed all 20 processed files in GEO series GSE193989 (10 cells x 2 parental genomes; columns chr,start_resolution,end_resolution,zaxis; 21,057-102,934 rows each; 254,937 unique 10 kb bins in the union). Downloaded the Sequential-GAM GitHub repository tree (84 files) and inspected its only example cell's 3D coordinate file (chr1_10kb_location_data_overlap.txt, 9,560 bins, x/y/z) plus one NP (nuclear profile) and one distance file. Ran two checks of my own: (1) cross-cell reproducibility of the depth coordinate after per-cell centring - median Spearman correlation 0.01 at 1 Mb bins across all 45 cell pairs, maximum 0.09; (2) a positive control against mouse gene density per 1 Mb from UCSC refGene - median Spearman 0.08 with the wrong sign and inconsistent across cells.",
    "what_came_from_paper_text_only": "That only 10 cells were produced in two batches, the 200 nm section thickness, the 4.3975 um nuclear radius, and the reconstruction recipe (constitutive lamina-associated domain fragments forced to within 0.5 um of the nuclear periphery, remaining loci placed by maximum likelihood under a power-law distance prior). Supplementary tables were not retrievable: the Europe PMC supplementaryFiles endpoint timed out on two attempts, and the NCBI GEO web page is behind a browser challenge (the FTP listing worked instead)."
  },
  "part_a_killers": {
    "a1_downloadable": {"pass": true, "note": "GEO GSE193989 processed CSV files download freely over FTP (20 files, 0.16-0.88 MB each) and the code repository is public; no login or application needed."},
    "a2_label_is_a_column": {"pass": false, "note": "FAIL. The paper's quantity of interest - radial distance of a locus from the nuclear centre - is not a column anywhere in the download. The only per-locus number is 'zaxis', the depth of the cryosection stack in micrometres (cell-specific offsets: 0.79-2.99 for one cell, 7.14-8.54 for another), which is a coordinate in the arbitrary cutting frame, not a radius. Getting the paper's label would mean re-running their Python 2.7 / TensorFlow 1.13 maximum-likelihood reconstruction on raw sequencing reads; only one example cell's chromosome 1 coordinates are published."},
    "a3_inputs_present": {"pass": true, "note": "Inputs would be mm10 genomic coordinates, which are present and standard; DNA sequence and mouse embryonic stem cell epigenomic tracks are fetchable separately."},
    "a4_units_stated": {"pass": false, "note": "The CSV files have no units column, no header documentation and no README; micrometres is only inferable from the methods text (200 nm sections, 4.3975 um radius) and from values falling on a 0.2 um grid."},
    "a5_enough_rows": {"pass": false, "n_rows": 254937, "note": "254,937 unique 10 kb bins looks ample, but the independent unit is the cell and there are 10 of them, all one cell line (mouse embryonic stem cell F123), one lab, two batches; the authors state each cell costs about USD 1200 and two days."},
    "a6_fits_laptop": {"pass": true, "working_set": "~10 MB compressed, ~120 MB in memory as a pandas table", "note": "Verified: all 20 files loaded and cross-correlated on a laptop in under a minute."},
    "a7_counts_match_paper": {"pass": true, "note": "Paper says 10 cells in two batches; GEO has 127 section-level samples and exactly 20 processed files = 10 cells x 2 parental genomes. Consistent."},
    "a8_label_provenance": {"pass": false, "note": "FAIL. Where radial positions do exist they are the output of the authors' own inference, which injects constitutive lamina-associated domain annotations (forced within 0.5 um of the periphery) and a power-law genomic-distance-to-spatial-distance prior. A sequence or epigenomics model predicting that label would partly be rediscovering the annotation the authors fed in - circularity plus leakage by construction."
  },
  "part_a_verdict": "reject",
