  "label_elsewhere": null,
  "leakage_plan": null,
  "success_criteria": null,
  "publication_target": null,
  "pitch": null,
  "ml_idea": "The intended project was: embed each 10 kb mm10 window with a DNA language model, freeze it, and fit a head predicting the window's radial distance from the nuclear centre, held out by chromosome, with cross-cell variance as a second target. It dies because the radial distance is not in the deposited data - only the cryosection depth coordinate is - and the version that does exist was built with lamina annotations injected as constraints.",
  "effort": {"hours_to_feature_table": 40, "working_set_gb": 0.12, "needs_gpu": false, "peak_ram_gb": 2, "embedding_hours": 60, "cv_run_minutes": 20, "compute_note": "Timed the actual data handling: all 20 files load and cross-correlate in under a minute at about 0.12 GB of RAM. The 40 hours and 60 embedding hours are estimates for the DNA-language-model route over roughly 255,000 windows on CPU, not measured.", "cheapest_killing_check": "Open one zlocation CSV and ask whether any column is the radial distance from the nuclear centre. It is not - it is the cryosection depth in the cutting frame, with a different offset in every cell. Second cheapest: correlate the centred depth with gene density (I got a median Spearman of 0.08 with inconsistent sign across cells, so the expected radial gradient is not recoverable from the deposited numbers)."},
  "verdict": "reject",
  "verdict_reason": "Fails A2 and A8. The paper's headline quantity - radial distance of each genomic region from the nuclear centre - is not a column in the public download; the only per-locus number is the cryosection depth in each cell's arbitrary cutting frame, and reconstructing the radial position would mean re-running a Python 2.7 / TensorFlow 1.13 maximum-likelihood pipeline that forces known lamina-associated regions to the periphery, making any sequence-based model partly circular. Two checks I ran confirm the deposited numbers are unusable as a label: cross-cell agreement on the depth coordinate is a median Spearman of 0.01 across all 45 cell pairs, and the gene-density positive control comes out at 0.08 with the wrong sign. Compounding this, the independent unit is the cell and there are only 10, all from one mouse embryonic stem cell line in one lab, and the files carry no units or column documentation."
}
